; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Layered Mandala
; CATEGORY: Patterns & Mandalas
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     mandala, symmetry, procedures as data, run, filled
; SUMMARY:  Builds a mandala from the inside out, one ring at a time, each ring a different motif repeated round the circle.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   A mandala is a circle pattern with the same thing repeated all
;   the way round. Here it is built in layers: a dotted center,
;   petals, a ring of diamonds, scalloped arches, teardrops and an
;   outer ring of dots. Each layer is described by one line in the
;   LAYERS list: which motif, how many, how far out, what color.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Edit the LAYERS list to design your own mandala:
;   change counts, distances or colors, or remove a layer.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * describing a design as data (a list of layers)
;   * RUN with a list built from a procedure name and its inputs
;   * motifs that start and end at the same place and heading
;   * painting in layers, where later shapes cover earlier ones
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Use 8 in every layer for a calm look, or 7 and 11 for a busy one.
;   * Write a new motif, for example a little star, and add a layer.
;   * Change the background to white and the colors to black.
; ============================================================

; Each motif is drawn pointing away from the center, starting at the
; point nearest the center, and returns there facing the same way.

to petal :size :color
  filled :color [
    repeat 2 [
      repeat 15 [forward :size / 12 right 4]
      right 120
    ]
  ]
end

to diamond :size :color
  filled :color [
    left 30 forward :size right 60 forward :size
    right 120 forward :size right 60 forward :size
    right 150
  ]
end

; a half circle arch, open side toward the center
to arch :size :color
  left 90 penup forward :size / 2 pendown right 90
  filled :color [repeat 18 [forward :size * 0.087 right 10] right 90 forward :size right 90]
  left 90 penup back :size / 2 pendown right 90
end

; a teardrop: a point toward the center and a round top. The two
; straight sides open 40 degrees apart; the top is an arc that turns
; 220 degrees, just enough to come back down the other side.
to teardrop :size :color
  filled :color [
    right 20 forward :size
    repeat 22 [forward :size * 0.0635 left 10]
    forward :size
    right 200
  ]
end

to spot :size :color
  penup forward :size / 2
  setpencolor :color setpensize :size dot pos
  back :size / 2 pendown
  setpensize 2 setpencolor [30 20 40]
end

; Put :count copies of a motif round the center at distance :r.
to layer :motif :count :r :size :color
  repeat :count [
    penup home right 360 * (repcount - 0.5) / :count forward :r pendown
    run (list :motif :size :color)
  ]
end

; [motif count distance size color], drawn in this order. Later drawing
; covers earlier drawing, so each ring of spots comes after the shapes
; it touches, and sits on top of them.
make "layers [
  [teardrop 16 182 62 [70 160 170]]
  [spot 36 270 12 [250 210 120]]
  [arch 24 148 36 [230 120 60]]
  [diamond 12 72 40 [240 190 60]]
  [petal 10 16 52 [200 60 100]]
  [spot 8 10 10 [250 230 180]]
]

to mandala
  foreach :layers [layer item 1 ? item 2 ? item 3 ? item 4 ? item 5 ?]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [30 20 40]
setpensize 2
setpencolor [30 20 40]
mandala
